# Thesis stages and current decisions

All three engineering components-ELMOS, HAVEN and KDAL-are required in the
final artifact. The runtime placement below is proposed and awaits review.
Stage 0 remains active; documentation and diagnostic experiments do not approve
runtime interfaces or production adoption.

The thesis stages are preparation (0), research decision (1), approved minimal
implementation (2), evaluation (3), and thesis/release (4). M0–M5 are separate
engineering work packages that can span those stages. Linux/vGIC, integrated
runs, physical validation and evaluation are not required to close Stage 0.
Known failures and unavailable boards can be recorded risks rather than closure
blockers; the exit checklist makes that distinction explicit.

| Read first | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| [Workspace instructions](../AGENTS.md) | Current scope, dependency authority, evidence and review rules |
| [Stage 0 baseline](STAGE0_BASELINE.md) | Observations, exact revisions and remaining feasibility gaps |
| [Stage 0 closure review](../haven/docs/methodology/stage0/20261025-closure/README.md) | Current closure checklist/recommendation, A1/A2 decisions, CP1 deferral and next bounded implementation proposal; no transition declared |
| [Current integrated design](../haven/docs/methodology/stage0/20261025-integration-design/README.md) | Required three-component artifact, proposed Linux/KDAL slice, contracts, milestones and first coordinated proposal |
| [Finding ledger](../haven/docs/methodology/stage0/20261025-corrections/FINDINGS.md) | Separate compiler, startup, IRQ and timer findings; use the new runtime addendum for subsequent evidence |
| [Correction review](../haven/docs/methodology/stage0/20261025-corrections/REVIEW.md) | Unapplied memcpy proposal and adoption gate |
| [Preserved boundary evidence](../haven/docs/methodology/stage0/20261025-boundaries/README.md) | Archived experiments and reproduction limits |

Earlier evidence packages preserve the scope and observations at their capture
date. Their statements that KDAL was optional, or that no integrated design was
defined, do not supersede the user's subsequent required-integration decision.
They still accurately record that no integrated runtime was observed then.

The integration roadmap's earlier statement that M0–M5 refined “Stage 0
integration work” is superseded by the separation above and its updated stage
mapping. Its original CP1 implementation-first sequence is superseded by the
closure review's recommendation to defer coordinated schema/CLI code until a
concrete artifact/architecture boundary needs it. Historical evidence and
proposal details remain available; those recommendations are not approvals.
